R-PA13 R-PA5 R-PA6 R-DI12 R-EC14 R-DI2 R-FE7 R-DI11 R-PA3 R-OUT2 (slice 070, a base that no release of the group has, and slice 070b, a base that a release has): 7 runs on 3 projects. p1 has json 2.2.0 in the header (it is in the cache) and a patch whose `base` is the hash of a json 2.1.5 that is not in the cache and that no release of the list has. The release list of acme/json (the fake HTTP, 3 releases: 2.1.0, 2.2.0, 2.3.0) is not in the index dir yet. `tln install` with no names applies the patch to the header release (R-PA6), so it needs the base for the diff (R-PA5).
Run 1 (`install --offline`): `packages/<base>` is missing (one `list_dirs` of it), so Talon looks for the base in the release list of the group. With `--offline` and no cached page there is no list: exit 15, the text of R-DI12 for a missing page (`Github.no_page_failure`). Run 2 (`install`): the list is requested (2 pages of the cache are written) and no release of the group (acme/json, series 2) has the hash: exit 14 (kind `frozen`), the text names the base, the alias and the 2 fixes of R-PA5 (`Patched.base_missing`). Nothing is written but the index pages: no copy, no `talon.toml`, no header, no temp dir. Run 3 (`install --offline`): the same exit 14 from the cached pages, and stderr has the line `index: cached at <time>` (R-DI12). The hash of a release of another group or repository is no release of the group (L0 `PatchedTest`). 
Slice 070b (R-PA13: a base that a release of the group has is fetched by its hash). p2 is p1 with the base of json 2.1.0 (DBH2...), a release of the list that is not in the cache. Run 4 (`install --offline`, p2): the base dir is missing, the cached list has a release with the hash, so Talon fetches it, and `--offline` stops in the fetch: exit 15, `acme/json 2.1.0 is not in the package cache and --offline is set (<url>)` (R-FE7, the text of any offline fetch), and the line `index: cached at <time>`. Run 5 (`patch json --diff`, p2, online): the same lookup (the list is requested again, no ETag), the fetch by hash (the fake download and `roc unbundle` of `fx/jobs`: the base files hold the text `fake`), then the 2 dirs are read and the diff of the copy against the base is printed (R-PA3), exit 0. The index pages and the base package are cache files that the command writes; the project has no change (R-PA3: `--diff` writes no file of the project). Run 6 (`patch json --diff`, p1, online): the base of p1 is the one that no release has, so `tln patch --diff` has the same missing-base rule as `install` (R-PA13, R-PA3): exit 14 with the text of `Patched.base_missing` (it was exit 18, `cannot read <dir>`).
Run 7 (`install --offline`, p3; slice 070b, manager answer Q1, R-PA13, R-DI11): p3 is p1 with a header release URL of another host (`example.org`: no `owner/repo`, so no release list can exist). The base is not in the cache, so the rule of R-PA13 gives exit 14 (kind `frozen`), also with `--offline`: it is not a missing cache (exit 15) and not `cannot read <dir>` (exit 18). The text is `Patched.base_missing` with the URL form of the group as the name: `no release of example.org/acme/json/releases/download/{v}/ has that hash` (a proposal, TW24). No request, no index call.
